{
	title: 'Replay tells the model what happened',
	spec: 'Provider input rebuilt from history must not garble or hide what happened. Today a turn that failed or was paused with no output leaves a user record, and replay.toMessages merges it with the next prompt into one message whose text blocks the provider joins with no separator ("Say just the word pong" + "k" was read as "pongk"). Fix it the way the old Hal does (reference: ~/.hal/src/server/session/api-messages.ts): each prompt stays its own user message, starting with a [HH:MM] line; how a turn ended (error, paused, continued after a restart) reaches the model as a short <meta> note in front of the next prompt. Test with the real replay of: an errored turn followed by a prompt, a paused turn followed by a prompt, and a normal two-turn history (which must not change).',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'replay.toMessages: a prompt record always starts a user message of its own, never merged; tool results (answered or made up) go in a message before it. So consecutive user messages are normal: Anthropic combines them server-side, openai-compat already splits results into tool messages. Text prompts start with `[HH:MM]` (replay.clock, host local time, the zone the system prompt date names) — `[YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM]` on the first prompt and whenever the date differs from the last stamped prompt\'s, so a stamp past midnight is not read as a stale system date; each stamp depends only on earlier records, so the cached prefix never changes — then the end note, joined by newlines into the first text block, not a separate block (providers join blocks with no separator).',
		'replay.endNote(turn_end) makes the note: error (message clipped to 500 chars), paused by Hal (pauseReason), interrupted (legacy), else paused by the user; completed gives none. A `continue` record drops the pending note: the continue note (or nothing) says it instead. Only the next prompt gets a note.',
		'Tests and fakes that read the prompt must strip the stamp: e2e.test.ts has bare(), host/history tests match /^\\[[\\d -]+:\\d\\d\\]\\n.../ (the date is optional).',
		'A transcript a client builds from a snapshot equals one it followed live: nothing marks where replayed history ends (task 66 removed the old resumed mark; the user did not want it).'
	],
	needs: ['j1'],
	foldInto: ['7']
}
